  "description": "A tiny lesson with a big payoff: When Neurons Die.",
  "is_free": false,
  "published": true,
  "story": {
    "hook": {
      "text": "You lose roughly 85,000 cortical neurons every day just from normal aging. Don't panic yet.",
      "visual": "📉"
    },
    "buildup": {
      "text": "With 86 billion to start, that daily loss barely registers over a typical lifetime.",
      "visual": "🧮"
    },
    "discovery": {
      "text": "The brain compensates by strengthening surviving connections—quality over quantity.",
      "visual": "💪"
    },
    "twist": {
      "text": "Neurodegenerative diseases accelerate loss catastrophically—Alzheimer's kills millions of neurons per year.",
      "visual": "🩺"
    },
    "climax": {
      "text": "Research into neuroprotection aims to slow or stop this loss before symptoms appear.",
      "visual": "🛡️"
    },
    "punchline": {
      "text": "Losing neurons is normal. Losing too many too fast is disease.",
      "visual": "⚕️"
    }
  },
  "quiz": {
    "question": "How does the aging brain compensate for neuron loss?",
    "options": [
      "By strengthening surviving connections",
      "By growing larger neurons",
      "By increasing skull size"
    ],
    "correct": 0
  },
